From f0f5efa30fe7ca59c47d957ace584b2294db4c90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:16:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 091/112] Filters: the SVF rounds instead of truncating and
 keeps its state precise at low cutoff; no sum wraps any more

SVF (spec points 2 and 3): every product in the recursion rounds (smmulr), the band's tanh interpolates the table to
all 24 bits and rounds (getTanHUnknown() dropped 8 bits: the band moved in floored steps of 32 LSB), and below fc
1/4 (~3.1 kHz) both integrators carry their state 32 bits below the LSB (smlal, as the LP ladders' precise stages);
sums and the output's tripling saturate. Against a float64 model (tests/filters svf_precision, cutoff 5 / 15): the
error's DC -88..-106 dBFS -> -175..-228, A-weighted error -154..-171 -> -184..-189 dBFS, the tail after the music
stuck at -101..-133 dBFS -> -178 (a rounded half LSB, tripled).

Ladders (spec point 3): the all-pass output 2b - x, the outputs' doubling, the feedback sums' and scaleInput's shifts
and differences, the morph term and the HP ladder's normalisation (<< 7) saturate instead of wrapping to the other
end. Bit-exact wherever nothing reached full scale: in filter_neutral's static cases only the SVF ones change (its
rounding) and the HP ladder with morph: its cutoff modulation took input << 4, which wrapped from -24 dBFS on (the
music there peaks above it) and now saturates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
